// NEGATIVE TEST — a GUARDED wildcard does not exhaust anything (N6-09 / N6-10).
//
// `_ if cond` is taken only sometimes, and which times is not decidable from the
// pattern, so it counts toward completeness exactly as much as any other guarded
// arm: not at all. A match whose only arm is a guarded wildcard is therefore
// non-exhaustive, and refusing it is the difference between a program that falls
// out of its `match` and one that never compiles.
fn main() {
    let v = match 4 {
        _ if 1 > 0 => 1,
    };
    print_int(v);
}
